From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:47:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: study slack sources for virtual timing-driven re-weights
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Study only, selected by environment variables, default unchanged:

GPL_TD_SLACKS picks where a virtual re-weight's slacks come from:
  rsz   repair_design and fullyRebuffer, OpenSTA, journal restore (today)
  sta   OpenSTA on the placement as it is (Resizer::findPlacementSlacks)
  fast  FastTimer: one OpenSTA run gives the graph, clock arrivals and
        endpoint required times; each re-weight then recomputes cell
        (NLDM) and wire (Elmore, set_wire_rc) delays from the current
        locations and propagates level by level over flat arrays with
        OpenMP, bit-identical at any thread count.

GPL_TD_COMPARE logs, at every virtual re-weight, the three sources'
rankings on the same placement against rsz's (top 1% and 10% overlap,
slack correlation) and what each costs (GPL-9913, GPL-9914). GPL-9911
logs each re-weight's wall time.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
